    <div class="legacy-poster">
        <div class="wrap">
            <div class="hub">
                <div class="hub-box">
                    <div class="hub-title">IAS 38 — Intangible assets</div>
                    <div class="hub-sub">
                        Recognition · Internally generated (R&amp;D) ·
                        Subsequent measurement · Amortisation &amp;
                        derecognition · Comprehensive comparison &amp;
                        interactions
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="grid">
                <!-- 01 Recognition & Initial Measurement -->
                <div class="card ci">
                    <div class="cnum">01</div>
                    <div class="ctitle ci">
                        Recognition &amp; initial measurement
                    </div>
                    <div class="principle">
                        An intangible asset is an <strong
                            style="font-weight:600">identifiable</strong
                        > non-monetary asset without physical substance. Three tests
                        must all be met before recognition.
                    </div>

                    <div class="elabel">THREE RECOGNITION TESTS</div>
                    <div class="dot-list" style="margin-bottom:9px;">
                        <span
                            ><strong style="font-weight:600"
                                >Identifiability</strong
                            > — separable (can be sold/licensed) OR arises from contractual/legal
                            rights</span
                        >
                        <span
                            ><strong style="font-weight:600">Control</strong> — entity
                            can obtain benefits and restrict others' access</span
                        >
                        <span
                            ><strong style="font-weight:600"
                                >Economic benefit + measurability</strong
                            > — probable future inflows, cost reliably measurable</span
                        >
                    </div>

                    <div class="div"></div>
                    <div class="elabel">
                        JOURNAL ENTRIES — INITIAL RECOGNITION
                    </div>
                    <div class="eg">
                        <div class="egl">
                            Separate acquisition (or from a business combination
                            at FV)
                        </div>
                        <div class="entry">
                            <span class="dr">Dr</span>
                            <div class="etxt">
                                Intangible asset — at cost / FV
                                <div class="badges">
                                    <span class="badge bs"
                                        >SOFP — non-current assets</span
                                    >
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="entry">
                            <span class="cr">Cr</span>
                            <div class="etxt">
                                Cash / payables (or goodwill in IFRS 3)
                                <div class="badges">
                                    <span class="badge bs">SOFP</span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="callout info" style="margin-bottom:0;">
                         <strong style="font-weight:600"
                            >Business combinations override the "no internal
                            recognition" rule:</strong
                        > an intangible acquired in a business combination is recognised
                        SEPARATELY from goodwill at fair value — even if the ACQUIREE
                        never recognised it (e.g. an unrecognised customer list or
                        brand). This is the one situation where an otherwise-prohibited
                        intangible (Card 02) suddenly becomes recognisable.
                    </div>
                    <div class="note">
                        No SOPL impact at initial recognition.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- 02 Internally Generated — Research vs Development -->
                <div class="card cs">
                    <div class="cnum">02</div>
                    <div class="ctitle cs">
                        Internally generated intangibles — R&amp;D
                    </div>
                    <div class="principle">
                        Expenditure must be classified into a research phase and
                        a development phase. Research is always expensed.
                        Development is capitalised only if all six criteria are
                        met.
                    </div>

                    <div class="elabel">RESEARCH PHASE — always expense</div>
                    <div class="entry">
                        <span class="dr">Dr</span>
                        <div class="etxt">
                            Research expense
                            <div class="badges">
                                <span class="badge bp"
                                    >SOPL — operating expense</span
                                >
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="entry">
                        <span class="cr">Cr</span>
                        <div class="etxt">
                            Cash / payables
                            <div class="badges">
                                <span class="badge bs">SOFP</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="div"></div>
                    <div class="elabel">
                        DEVELOPMENT PHASE — capitalise if ALL six criteria met
                        (PIRATE)
                    </div>
                    <div class="dot-list" style="margin-bottom:7px;">
                        <span
                            ><strong style="font-weight:600">P</strong> — Probable
                            future economic benefits</span
                        >
                        <span
                            ><strong style="font-weight:600">I</strong> — Intention
                            to complete and use/sell</span
                        >
                        <span
                            ><strong style="font-weight:600">R</strong> — Resources
                            adequate to complete</span
                        >
                        <span
                            ><strong style="font-weight:600">A</strong> — Ability
                            to use or sell the asset</span
                        >
                        <span
                            ><strong style="font-weight:600">T</strong> — Technical
                            feasibility of completion</span
                        >
                        <span
                            ><strong style="font-weight:600">E</strong> — Expenditure
                            reliably measurable</span
                        >
                    </div>
                    <div class="entry">
                        <span class="dr">Dr</span>
                        <div class="etxt">
                            Development costs (intangible asset)
                            <div class="badges">
                                <span class="badge bs">SOFP — NCAs</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="entry">
                        <span class="cr">Cr</span>
                        <div class="etxt">
                            Cash / payables
                            <div class="badges">
                                <span class="badge bs">SOFP</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="callout danger" style="margin-bottom:8px;">
                         <strong style="font-weight:600"
                            >Once expensed, it can NEVER be reinstated</strong
                        > as an asset in a later period — even if the criteria are
                        subsequently met. This is a one-way door, frequently tested.
                    </div>

                    <div class="elabel">
                        CANNOT EVER BE RECOGNISED (IAS 38.63)
                    </div>
                    <div class="cross-list">
                        <span>Internally generated goodwill</span>
                        <span>Internally generated brands &amp; mastheads</span>
                        <span>Publishing titles &amp; customer lists</span>
                        <span>Start-up, training &amp; advertising costs</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="note">
                        Website development costs (SIC-32): planning stage =
                        expense; application/infrastructure development stage =
                        capitalise if the six criteria are met, same as any
                        other development cost.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- 03 Subsequent Measurement -->
                <div class="card cw">
                    <div class="cnum">03</div>
                    <div class="ctitle cw">Subsequent measurement</div>
                    <div class="principle">
                        Choose cost model or revaluation model as an accounting
                        policy. Revaluation is only possible where an active
                        market exists — which is rare for intangibles.
                    </div>

                    <div class="elabel">COST MODEL (most common)</div>
                    <div
                        style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-bottom:8px;line-height:1.6;"
                    >
                        Carrying amount = Cost − Accumulated amortisation −
                        Accumulated impairment losses
                    </div>

                    <div class="div"></div>
                    <div class="elabel">
                        REVALUATION MODEL (requires active market — rare)
                    </div>
                    <div class="eg">
                        <div class="egl">
                            Upward revaluation — no prior deficit on this asset
                        </div>
                        <div class="entry">
                            <span class="dr">Dr</span>
                            <div class="etxt">
                                Intangible asset — increase to FV
                                <div class="badges">
                                    <span class="badge bs">SOFP — NCAs</span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="entry">
                            <span class="cr">Cr</span>
                            <div class="etxt">
                                Revaluation surplus
                                <div class="badges">
                                    <span class="badge bo">OCI</span><span
                                        class="badge be">SOFP — equity</span
                                    >
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="eg">
                        <div class="egl">
                            Downward revaluation — no prior surplus on this
                            asset
                        </div>
                        <div class="entry">
                            <span class="dr">Dr</span>
                            <div class="etxt">
                                Revaluation loss
                                <div class="badges">
                                    <span class="badge bp">SOPL — expense</span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="entry">
                            <span class="cr">Cr</span>
                            <div class="etxt">
                                Intangible asset — decrease to FV
                                <div class="badges">
                                    <span class="badge bs">SOFP — NCAs</span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="callout warn" style="margin-bottom:0;">
                         <strong style="font-weight:600"
                            >Active markets for intangibles are genuinely rare</strong
                        > — taxi licences and some tradeable production quotas are
                        common exam examples; brands, customer lists, and patents
                        almost never qualify, because each is unique. If the active
                        market later ceases to exist, the LAST revalued amount becomes
                        deemed cost going forward, and the entity reverts to the cost
                        model.
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- 04 Amortisation & Derecognition -->
                <div class="card cd">
                    <div class="cnum">04</div>
                    <div class="ctitle cd">
                        Amortisation &amp; derecognition
                    </div>
                    <div class="principle">
                        The useful life assessment drives everything. A finite
                        life triggers systematic amortisation through SOPL; an
                        indefinite life means no amortisation but a mandatory
                        annual impairment test instead.
                    </div>

                    <div class="two-col" style="margin-bottom:9px;">
                        <div>
                            <span class="tag tag-finite"
                                >Finite useful life</span
                            >
                            <div class="entry">
                                <span class="dr">Dr</span>
                                <div class="etxt">
                                    Amortisation expense
                                    <div class="badges">
                                        <span class="badge bp"
                                            >SOPL — expense</span
                                        >
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div class="entry">
                                <span class="cr">Cr</span>
                                <div class="etxt">
                                    Accumulated amortisation
                                    <div class="badges">
                                        <span class="badge bs"
                                            >SOFP — reduces CA</span
                                        >
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <span class="tag tag-indef"
                                >Indefinite useful life</span
                            >
                            <div
                                style="font-size:11px;color:var(--color-text-secondary);line-height:1.6;"
                            >
                                No amortisation charge. Mandatory ANNUAL
                                impairment test under IAS 36 — regardless of
                                whether indicators exist.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="div"></div>
                    <div class="elabel">DERECOGNITION — JOURNAL ENTRIES</div>
                    <div class="entry">
                        <span class="dr">Dr</span>
                        <div class="etxt">
                            Accumulated amortisation
                            <div class="badges">
                                <span class="badge bs"
                                    >SOFP — clears credit balance</span
                                >
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="entry">
                        <span class="dr">Dr</span>
                        <div class="etxt">
                            Cash / receivable (proceeds)
                            <div class="badges">
                                <span class="badge bs">SOFP</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="entry">
                        <span class="dr">Dr</span>
                        <div class="etxt">
                            <span
                                style="color:var(--color-text-tertiary);font-size:10px;"
                                >[if loss]</span
                            > Loss on disposal
                            <div class="badges">
                                <span class="badge bp">SOPL — expense</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="entry">
                        <span class="cr">Cr</span>
                        <div class="etxt">
                            Intangible asset — at cost
                            <div class="badges">
                                <span class="badge bs">SOFP — NCAs</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="entry">
                        <span class="cr">Cr</span>
                        <div class="etxt">
                            <span
                                style="color:var(--color-text-tertiary);font-size:10px;"
                                >[if gain]</span
                            > Gain on disposal
                            <div class="badges">
                                <span class="badge bp">SOPL — income</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="note">
                        Revaluation surplus on disposal: Dr Revaluation surplus
                        / Cr Retained earnings — bypasses SOPL, mirroring IAS
                        16. Review useful life, residual value and method at
                        least annually (IAS 8 — change in estimate, applied
                        prospectively).
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- 05 Comprehensive Comparison & Key Interactions — full width -->
                <div class="card cn span2">
                    <div class="cnum">05</div>
                    <div class="ctitle cn">
                        Comprehensive comparison &amp; key interactions with
                        other standards
                    </div>

                    <div class="two-col">
                        <div>
                            <div class="elabel">
                                COMPREHENSIVE COMPARISON — IAS 38 vs IAS 16
                            </div>
                            <div class="td-table" style="margin-bottom:10px;">
                                <div
                                    class="th"
                                    style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr 1fr;"
                                >
                                    <span>Feature</span><span
                                        style="color:var(--color-text-info);"
                                        >IAS 38</span
                                    ><span
                                        style="color:var(--color-text-success);"
                                        >IAS 16</span
                                    >
                                </div>
                                <div
                                    class="tr"
                                    style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr 1fr;"
                                >
                                    <span>Recognition test</span><span
                                        >Identifiability + control + benefit</span
                                    ><span
                                        >Probable benefit + reliable cost</span
                                    >
                                </div>
                                <div
                                    class="tr alt"
                                    style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr 1fr;"
                                >
                                    <span>Internally generated?</span><span
                                        >Mostly PROHIBITED</span
                                    ><span
                                        >Self-constructed assets ARE capitalised</span
                                    >
                                </div>
                                <div
                                    class="tr"
                                    style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr 1fr;"
                                >
                                    <span>Indefinite life option</span><span
                                        >Yes (unique to IAS 38)</span
                                    ><span
                                        >No — always depreciated (except land)</span
                                    >
                                </div>
                                <div
                                    class="tr alt"
                                    style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr 1fr;"
                                >
                                    <span>Revaluation model</span><span
                                        >Rare (needs active market)</span
                                    ><span>Common in practice</span>
                                </div>
                                <div
                                    class="tr"
                                    style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr 1fr;"
                                >
                                    <span>Components approach</span><span
                                        >Not applicable</span
                                    ><span>Mandatory for significant parts</span
                                    >
                                </div>
                            </div>

                            <div class="elabel">
                                CLASSIFICATION EXAMPLES — WHAT GOES WHERE
                            </div>
                            <div class="td-table">
                                <div
                                    class="th"
                                    style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr;"
                                >
                                    <span>Item</span><span>Treatment</span>
                                </div>
                                <div
                                    class="tr"
                                    style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr;"
                                >
                                    <span>Purchased patent</span><span
                                        style="color:var(--color-text-success);"
                                        >Recognise, finite life</span
                                    >
                                </div>
                                <div
                                    class="tr alt"
                                    style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr;"
                                >
                                    <span>Internally generated brand</span><span
                                        style="color:var(--color-text-danger);"
                                        >Never recognise</span
                                    >
                                </div>
                                <div
                                    class="tr"
                                    style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr;"
                                >
                                    <span
                                        >Customer list acquired in a business
                                        combination</span
                                    ><span
                                        style="color:var(--color-text-success);"
                                        >Recognise separately from goodwill</span
                                    >
                                </div>
                                <div
                                    class="tr alt"
                                    style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr;"
                                >
                                    <span
                                        >Taxi licence (renewable, tradeable)</span
                                    ><span
                                        style="color:var(--color-text-warning);"
                                        >Indefinite life — no amortisation</span
                                    >
                                </div>
                                <div
                                    class="tr"
                                    style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr;"
                                >
                                    <span>Staff training costs</span><span
                                        style="color:var(--color-text-danger);"
                                        >Expense — never an asset</span
                                    >
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <div>
                            <div class="elabel">
                                KEY INTERACTIONS WITH OTHER STANDARDS
                            </div>
                            <div class="dot-list" style="margin-bottom:10px;">
                                <span
                                    ><strong style="font-weight:600"
                                        >IFRS 3</strong
                                    > — business combinations force recognition of
                                    intangibles the acquiree never recognised itself,
                                    separately from goodwill, at fair value</span
                                >
                                <span
                                    ><strong style="font-weight:600"
                                        >IAS 36</strong
                                    > — indefinite-life and not-yet-available-for-use
                                    intangibles require a MANDATORY annual impairment
                                    test, regardless of indicators; finite-life intangibles
                                    follow the normal indicator-based test</span
                                >
                                <span
                                    ><strong style="font-weight:600"
                                        >IAS 20</strong
                                    > — government grants toward an intangible asset
                                    either reduce its cost or are recognised as deferred
                                    income, released in line with amortisation</span
                                >
                                <span
                                    ><strong style="font-weight:600"
                                        >IAS 23</strong
                                    > — borrowing costs may be capitalised into a
                                    qualifying intangible asset under development
                                    (e.g. a long-construction software platform)</span
                                >
                                <span
                                    ><strong style="font-weight:600"
                                        >IFRS 15</strong
                                    > — costs to obtain or fulfil a customer contract
                                    may be capitalised as a contract asset under IFRS
                                    15 rather than as an IAS 38 intangible, if they
                                    meet IFRS 15's own criteria instead</span
                                >
                            </div>

                            <div class="elabel">COMMON EXAM TRAPS</div>
                            <div class="dot-list">
                                <span
                                    ><strong style="font-weight:600"
                                        >R&amp;D boundary:</strong
                                    > failing to correctly identify where research
                                    ends and development begins within a single project</span
                                >
                                <span
                                    ><strong style="font-weight:600"
                                        >Reinstatement:</strong
                                    > trying to capitalise previously expensed development
                                    costs once criteria are later met</span
                                >
                                <span
                                    ><strong style="font-weight:600"
                                        >Indefinite ≠ infinite:</strong
                                    > indefinite life means "no foreseeable limit,"
                                    not "never amortise under any circumstance" —
                                    reassess every period</span
                                >
                                <span
                                    ><strong style="font-weight:600"
                                        >Business combination override:</strong
                                    > forgetting that the "no internal recognition"
                                    rule does not apply to a business combination
                                    — those intangibles ARE recognised separately
                                    at fair value</span
                                >
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="legend">
                <div class="ltitle">Financial statement key</div>
                <div class="lrow">
                    <span class="badge bs">SOFP</span> Statement of financial position
                    (balance sheet)
                    <span class="badge bp">SOPL</span> Statement of profit or loss
                    (income statement)
                    <span class="badge bo">OCI</span> Other comprehensive income
                    <span class="badge be">Equity</span> SOFP — equity section (retained
                    earnings / revaluation surplus)
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
